A continuation paragraph lines up under the item CONTENT, at column 2 for
a `- ` marker, and not past the checkbox.

The checkbox stands inside the content, so it shifts nothing after it.
Counting its width put the continuation at column 6, which is four columns
past the content start and therefore an indented code block: the author's
prose stopped being prose after one pass, and drifted four more columns on
every pass after that.

Two other defects show in the same fixture. Before the tasklist extension
was attached the box came back as `\[ \]`, and the two paragraphs of the
item were run together with nothing between them, welding "release" onto
"Wait".

The `then-args` pass formats the first pass again, so a drift of even one
column fails this case.
